from more murderous games we never got  to see to alternate costumes characters  and casting squid game was almost  completely different yupikai movie  lovers i'm jan and in this video i'm  revealing everything that was deleted  cut or changed in the final version of  squid game obviously spoilers ahead so  take care  when the show's creator first came up  with a concept for squid game back in  2008 he wanted to make a feature-length  movie not a tv series the original  script was for a two-hour film and  although it mainly concentrated on the  games rather than the relationships  between characters and their backstories  there still wasn't enough screen time to  cover all the games we see in the show  today in fact even when it came to the  netflix series there was still a whole  bunch of korean children's games they  considered including but that ended up  getting the chop for instance there's  gongy which consists of throwing into  the air catching and picking up pebbles  or other small objects not only is it  popular in korea but it's also found in  countries around the world under a  variety of names including knuckle bones  or jacks another game the creator almost  included but decided to cut was a game  based on a korean nursery rhyme that's  similar to oranges and lemons or london  bridges falling down where children form  arches or gates with their arms which  they drop to catch players walking  underneath as the song finishes i can  imagine the horrific twist the show  might have added to this game given how  the nursery rhyme ending of oranges and  lemons is a chopper coming to chop off  your head a team game that almost made  it into the series was why did you come  to my house where players hold hands in  two lines and advance on each other  trying to win players from the other  side over to their own it's a bit like  the game red rover but the korean  version also involves a song and rock  paper scissors originally instead of the  red and blue tile game that the salesman  plays with gyun the show's creator  thought they should play a kind of  knitting game called cat's cradle it's a  game where the players create string  figures between their fingers and he  thought it would be funny to see two men  doing that however he said he gave up on  the idea as the rules wouldn't be  understood globally elastics or jump  rope was also suggested but he felt that  didn't work in terms of excitement and  tension and was a little difficult for  everyone when it came to explaining all  the rules by the way gongy and elastics  did at least get a shout out in the show  when gion was speculating what game they  might play next  the distinctive costumes worn by the  characters are a crucial part of the  highly stylized series but originally  its creator wanted a completely  different look for the game's workers  which would have given them more of a  boy scout vibe now i can see where he  was coming from with that idea as boy  scouts are associated with childhood and  the whole show from its games to its  sets emphasizes the irony of grown-ups  playing kids games but with very adult  consequences however scout outfits  wouldn't have given the workers the same  degree of anonymity and they also  wouldn't have given them the sense of  being ants in an ant colony that the  director was looking for the show's art  director also went through numerous  takes on the worker's mask including  animal designs before arriving at the  final fencing inspired mask with lines  reminiscent of an ant's face the  ultimate design of hot pink hooded  jumpsuits with black masks has proven  hugely popular around the world with  store-bought versions selling like  hotcakes or should that be honeycombs  and becoming a top choice for halloween  some of the most heartbreaking moments  in the marbles game were originally  going to be very different in the early  days of squid game's development as a  movie g young as we know her didn't  exist and rather than a young woman  who'd been imprisoned for killing her  abusive father in her place was a male  character however 10 years later when  writer director wang dong-yuk came to  adapt his original idea for tv he  decided to create a female character  instead as he wanted to develop a bond  between her and north korean defector  sebioc and highlight two people who  weren't fighting and killing each other  to climb up despite their gut-wrenching  life or death situation the scenes  between jiyong and her partner in the  marbles game with all their empathy and  understanding are among the most  powerful and touching moments in the  series and have had viewers the world  over in tears in fact just reading the  script for that episode had the actress  who played stabiliuk sobbing her heart  out and as far as the show's creator is  concerned those two characters are in a  way the most innocent people and ji  young sacrificing herself so sabiak can  reunite with her family is the scene  that makes you cry the most  another fan favorite performance we  almost missed out on was anu  pomtrapati's portrayal of pakistani  migrant worker ali abdul who ends up in  the games as he can't support his family  after his boss repeatedly refuses to pay  his wages although ali is played  beautifully by trapati apparently he  wasn't the original choice for the role  that was actually filipino actor carlo  aquino who the show's creator invited to  audition after seeing him in a filipino  movie but despite being offered the part  of ali sadly for aquino covered 19  restrictions prevented him from  traveling to korea for the shoot so the  production looked at foreign performers  already in the country which is how  indian actor trapati who moved there 11  years ago got his chance to impress the  team with his emotional acting and  fluency in korean three auditions later  he got his big breakthrough and went on  to capture the hearts of millions with  his take on the kind and selfless ali  leaving many of us crying our eyes out  during his heart-rending final scenes by  the way another filipino actor christian  legahed also auditioned for ali but  while his acting was good they were  worried he wasn't fluent enough in  korean he did still end up in the show  though as player 276 who you can spot  taking part in the tug of war on gn's  team  as if having to play and win kids games  to stay alive wasn't bad enough the  players also have to contend with the  murderous bully doksu and his gang  including con artist migno who  interestingly enough weren't in the  original script for squid games  according to the show's creator he added  them to the netflix series as he wanted  a villain character to escalate conflict  in the initial movie script there was no  sign of policeman jun ho who in the  series poses as a worker to infiltrate  the games and find his missing brother  jun ho ends up being a crucial part of  the story as he gives viewers a  backstage pass to life behind the scenes  for both the workers and the vips thank  goodness then the show's creator was  able to add his character and storyline  once he had lots of extra screen time to  play with adapting his film idea for tv  combined with its eye-catching artwork  squid game is such an attention-grabbing  title for the show that it's hard to  imagine anyone ever thinking of calling  it anything else but in 2019 when  netflix first announced that they were  producing the series it had a totally  different name back then it was called  round six after the number of games  played according to min young kim the  netflix executive of the region that  name came about because they wanted the  show to appeal to audiences everywhere  and were worried not enough people would  get the title squid game what an odd  name as even in korea where it's a real  children's game apparently it's not well  known to every generation so initially  they thought the more general name round  six would help people understand what  the series was about fortunately the  writer director later steered them back  to his original title as it's a unique  show and that game is the essence of it  even worse than a title change for many  people though would have been if the  show had never been made and for a long  time that was a very real probability as  all the korean studios that creator wang  pitched his idea to back in 2008-9  thought that the whole concept was too  grotesque and unrealistic so finding  investors and actors for his script  which at the time was for a two-hour  movie proved impossible a decade later  however the show's writer-director says  that sadly the world has changed into a  place where such an unbelievable  survival story fits well and he added  that some elements even seem realistic  now that so many people are interested  in fast making money schemes and on top  of that the pandemic has exacerbated the  disparity between rich and poor in fact  he actually came up with the original  idea after the global financial crisis  of 2008 when three generations of his  own family were struggling for money and  living on loans after his mother retired  and a film he was working on fell  through indeed things were so bad that  at one point he had to stop writing the  script as he needed to sell his laptop  for cash a breakthrough came though in  2018 when he took his idea to netflix  who'd just recently opened an office in  seoul and they snapped up the project  suggesting they worked together to turn  it into a series as they felt there was  much more to the story than could be  contained in one movie a lot of hard  work later and squid game became south  korea's first series to reach netflix's  number one spot in the us and around the  world and the show's just full of  incredible details in the set design  plus tons of sneaky easter eggs and  foreshadowing for all the characters  which i discuss in lots more depth in my  things you missed video tap here to  watch that or follow 